/* LISTENING x2 (A) — Listen and Choose a Response : vie universitaire et académique (cours, labos, délais, conseillers, bibliothèque, logement, clubs, recherche, examens, projets de groupe, stages, bourses). Ajout via push. */
(function () {
  CONTENT.lcr.push(
    { id: "lza001", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "I'm afraid the data doesn't quite match the hypothesis.", o: ["That's still a result. Have you thought about what might explain the gap?","The match starts at three.","I'm afraid of heights, too.","The hypothesis was published a year ago, and it hasn't been challenged since then."], a: 0, x: "Mauvaise nouvelle scientifique : on la relativise. « Match » (adéquation) vs « match » (rencontre sportive)." },
    { id: "lza002", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "You wouldn't believe the queue at the financial aid office.", o: ["I wouldn't believe it either.","Financial aid is a good idea for anyone with student loans to pay off.","The queue at the cafeteria is longer.","Oh no. Is it worth going now, or should I try first thing tomorrow?"], a: 3, x: "Expression d'exaspération : on réagit et on pose une question utile. Pièges : écho." },
    { id: "lza003", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Our lab report is due Friday, and my partner still hasn't sent me his part.", o: ["Friday works for me. I'm free all afternoon.","Have you tried messaging him? He may simply have forgotten.","I've already sent my part to the lab assistant.","He was partly right about the lab report."], a: 1, x: "Problème exposé : on réagit au problème (relancer le partenaire). Les autres réponses parlent d'autre chose (disponibilité, sa propre partie)." },
    { id: "lza004", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "The exam covers chapters one through eight, doesn't it?", o: ["Yes, I have my chapters in my backpack.","The exam is held in the gymnasium.","Actually, I think chapter eight was left out. Let me check the syllabus.","It does cover a lot of ground, doesn't it?"], a: 2, x: "Tag question : on corrige poliment (« Actually »). Le dernier piège imite la structure sans répondre." },
    { id: "lza005", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Are there any rooms left in the graduate residence for the spring term?", o: ["The spring term starts in January.","The residence has a beautiful garden, and the rooms there are all quite spacious.","I graduated in the spring of last year.","I'm not sure. The housing office would know; they update the list on Mondays."], a: 3, x: "« I'm not sure » + orientation vers la bonne source. Les autres répètent « spring » ou « graduate »." },
    { id: "lza006", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "I just heard back from the housing office. They can't guarantee me a room.", o: ["Good for you. You'll love living in the dorms.","That's rough. Have you looked at off-campus options or a shared flat?","I heard back from them last week, and I got a room.","The guarantee on that laptop runs out in June."], a: 1, x: "Mauvaise nouvelle : empathie + piste. Les pièges ignorent le sens négatif ou jouent sur « guarantee »." },
    { id: "lza007", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "The abstract's due at noon, but the portal's been glitchy all morning.", o: ["Noon is when the portal opens, and it closes again at five every day for maintenance.","The portal is fine on my end. It opened right away.","Then email it as well, so you have a timestamp in case something goes wrong.","Noon is a reasonable deadline, honestly."], a: 2, x: "Risque technique : conseil de précaution. Pièges : mots répétés (« noon », « abstract »)." },
    { id: "lza008", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "The TA wasn't exactly thrilled when I asked for a regrade.", o: ["I can't say I'm surprised. He must get dozens of those requests.","Great, so he agreed to raise your grade.","The regrade should take about a week.","Then he'll probably be quick, since he enjoys regrading."], a: 0, x: "Litote : « wasn't exactly thrilled » = il était agacé. Le premier piège prend la phrase au pied de la lettre." },
    { id: "lza009", diff: 4, g: "W", p: "Considering how much he talked in seminar, you'd think he'd done the reading.", o: ["Yes, he must have read everything carefully, judging from that.","He considered reading it again, I suppose, but he's always been a slow reader anyway.","He talked a lot because he was well prepared, I think.","Funny, I had the same suspicion. His comments were pretty vague, weren't they?"], a: 3, x: "Ironie : « you'd think » suggère le contraire (il n'a pas lu). On partage le soupçon. Pièges : on croit à la préparation." },
    { id: "lza010", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Where should I hand in the lab form, to the TA or to the professor?", o: ["The form is available on the department website, along with the instructions for each lab.","The professor handed it in yesterday.","Either works, but the TA usually collects them at the start of class.","I think the lab starts at nine."], a: 2, x: "Question à choix : la bonne réponse précise l'usage. Les autres sont sur le thème (formulaire, laboratoire) mais ne répondent pas." },
    { id: "lza011", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "I'm up against two deadlines on Monday and a lab practical on Tuesday.", o: ["Monday is a good day for the practical, because the lab is usually nearly empty then.","Sounds like you've got your work cut out for you. Shall we map out a schedule?","I'm up at six every morning, too.","It's lucky the deadlines are so far off."], a: 1, x: "« Have your work cut out » = avoir fort à faire. Le dernier piège contredit le message (les échéances sont proches)." },
    { id: "lza012", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "I reckon we should aim for the early bird deadline for the conference.", o: ["Agreed. If we submit by the first, the registration fee is lower.","I'd rather submit late, since I'm not a morning person, to be honest.","I reckon the conference took place in June, but the proceedings came out later.","Our abstract is due in the spring, not before."], a: 0, x: "« Early bird deadline » = date limite à tarif réduit. Les pièges lisent l'expression au sens propre ou changent de temps." },
    { id: "lza013", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "We got the grant! Well, partly. They're funding the first year only.", o: ["Great, so the whole project is funded.","Partly is the part I like best.","My parents funded the first year of my degree, and I covered the rest with a part-time job.","Congratulations. That's a start. Shall we plan a follow-up proposal for the rest?"], a: 3, x: "« Well, partly » nuance la bonne nouvelle. Un piège ignore la restriction." },
    { id: "lza014", diff: 4, g: "M", p: "It's hardly surprising that the experiment failed, given how little time we had to design it.", o: ["Right, I'm surprised it worked with so little time. We must have been very lucky.","True, though I'd have liked to think we could pull it off anyway.","We had plenty of time to design it, so that's odd.","It was a surprise, since the design was so careful."], a: 1, x: "« Hardly surprising » = sans surprise. « Pull it off » = réussir. La bonne réponse concède avec regret. Pièges : contradiction (réussite, temps suffisant)." },
    { id: "lza015", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "You've got some nerve showing up late and then asking to copy my notes.", o: ["Fair enough. I'm sorry. I'll make it up to you with coffee.","Thanks. I stay calm under pressure.","I showed up at ten past nine.","Of course you can copy them. Here they are, and take as long as you need with them."], a: 0, x: "« You've got some nerve » = reproche. On s'excuse. Pièges : lecture littérale, réponse décalée du reproche." },
    { id: "lza016", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "I'm afraid I'll have to miss tomorrow's lab session. I have a dental appointment.", o: ["I have a dentist near the lab, too.","Tomorrow's session is about enzymes.","No problem. Just tell the instructor and ask about a make-up session.","That's why I always brush after lunch, and I floss every single night as well."], a: 2, x: "Annonce d'absence : réponse compréhensive et pratique. Les autres restent sur « dental » ou « lab » sans réagir." },
    { id: "lza017", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "I'm applying for the exchange program, but my GPA is a bit on the low side.", o: ["The exchange rate is low right now.","Don't let that put you off. A strong statement of purpose can make up for it.","Yes, the low side of the program is better.","I don't put much off, as you can see."], a: 1, x: "« Put someone off » = décourager ; « make up for » = compenser. Pièges : « exchange » (monnaie), « put off » littéral." },
    { id: "lza018", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "The reading list for this seminar is, frankly, a bit much.", o: ["It's much cheaper than buying the books new, if you can find used copies online.","Frank recommended most of those books.","I'm glad you enjoy long reading lists.","Tell me about it. I'm already two books behind, and it's only week three."], a: 3, x: "« A bit much » = excessif. « Tell me about it » signale l'accord. Pièges : contresens, jeu sur « Frank »." },
    { id: "lza019", diff: 4, g: "M", p: "It wasn't the worst feedback I've ever had, but it came close.", o: ["That's good news. It sounds like she was fairly positive.","I'm glad it was the best, then.","Ouch. Was there anything in it you can use?","It came close to the end of the semester, which is a shame."], a: 2, x: "Litote : « came close to the worst » = très dur. On compatit. Pièges : lecture positive, contresens." },
    { id: "lza020", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "I'm worried the survey won't get enough responses by the cutoff.", o: ["Why not send a reminder tomorrow and post a link in the student group chat?","Cut the survey down. It's far too long, and nobody wants to answer fifty questions.","The response was quick last year.","I'm worried about the cutoff for the scholarship."], a: 0, x: "Inquiétude : on propose une action. Pièges : répétition de « cut » et « worried »." },
    { id: "lza021", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "My roommate has been playing music until two in the morning, and I have an exam tomorrow.", o: ["Have you talked to her about it, or should we ask the resident advisor to step in?","Music helps me concentrate until about two.","Two roommates took the exam together.","It's been playing on the radio for two hours."], a: 0, x: "Plainte : on propose des étapes. Les pièges répètent « music », « two », « exam »." },
    { id: "lza022", diff: 4, g: "M", p: "The dean's office assured me my case would be looked into, which is bureaucrat-speak for nothing will happen.", o: ["That's good news. They'll be looking into it soon.","Looking into cases is exactly what the dean's office is for, so I'd just wait patiently.","I'm sure they meant it. They've always been helpful to me, to be honest.","Cynical, but fair. I'd follow up in writing so there's a record."], a: 3, x: "Cynisme : on le partage et on conseille un suivi écrit. Pièges : lecture naïve de l'assurance." },
    { id: "lza023", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "I'd been under the impression that attendance wasn't mandatory.", o: ["My impression of the lecture was good.","The attendance sheet was under the desk.","That's what I thought, too, but the syllabus says it counts for ten percent.","I didn't mandate anything in that class."], a: 2, x: "« Under the impression » = croire à tort. La bonne réponse partage l'erreur et la corrige avec un fait. Les autres jouent sur des mots isolés." },
    { id: "lza024", diff: 4, g: "M", p: "You'd have thought they'd learned from last year's registration fiasco.", o: ["They did learn. Registration went smoothly this time.","You'd think so, wouldn't you? The site crashed again within five minutes.","Last year's fiasco was a lesson for everyone involved.","Yes, I thought so too, and I learned a lot."], a: 1, x: "« You'd have thought » = on aurait cru (déception). La bonne réponse confirme l'échec répété. Pièges : contradiction, généralité." },
    { id: "lza025", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "I'd appreciate it if you could keep the noise down in the lab. Some of us are trying to concentrate.", o: ["The lab is down the hall, but the noise doesn't reach the offices from there.","Sorry about that. We'll wrap up and take the conversation outside.","No problem. I'll turn the music down in my room tonight, to be honest.","The noise was louder in the dorm last night."], a: 1, x: "Demande polie déguisée : on s'excuse et on obtempère. Pièges : « noise » réutilisé." },
    { id: "lza026", diff: 4, g: "M", p: "I can't decide whether to be flattered or insulted that he asked me to proofread his thesis at the last minute.", o: ["Probably a bit of both. Are you going to do it?","Thanks for the compliment. I'd be happy to proofread yours, too.","He asked me last week, and I finished it yesterday.","He proofread mine at the last minute, too, so we're even."], a: 0, x: "Sentiments mêlés : « Probably a bit of both » enchaîne naturellement. Les pièges choisissent un camp ou racontent une autre histoire." },
    { id: "lza027", diff: 4, g: "M", p: "My advisor's idea of feedback is a thumbs-up emoji.", o: ["Well, a thumbs-up is a good sign. She obviously approves of the draft.","Maybe you could send her an emoji to say thanks.","That's not much to go on. Have you asked her for more detail?","At least you get a reply. Mine takes weeks to answer."], a: 2, x: "Sarcasme : « my advisor's idea of feedback » = un retour très insuffisant. Les pièges y voient un éloge, ou changent de sujet (remerciement, comparaison)." },
    { id: "lza028", diff: 4, g: "W", p: "Don't take this the wrong way, but your introduction rambles a bit.", o: ["I wouldn't take it that way. My introduction is quite short.","I took the wrong way, didn't I? Sorry about that.","I'm sorry you think so, but I'm happy with it as it is.","No, that's useful. Where do you think I should cut it?"], a: 3, x: "« Don't take this the wrong way » prépare une critique. La bonne réponse l'accepte et demande des précisions. Pièges : réaction défensive ou mauvais sujet." },
    { id: "lza029", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "Heads up: the lab inspection is on Thursday, so don't leave anything lying around.", o: ["Thanks for the warning. I'll tidy my bench before I leave tomorrow.","I'll keep my head up, don't worry.","The lab was inspected last Thursday.","Lying around is exactly what I'd like to do."], a: 0, x: "« Heads up » = avertissement. Pièges : lecture littérale, mauvais temps, jeu sur « lying around »." },
    { id: "lza030", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "How are you planning to fund the final year of your degree?", o: ["The final year starts in September, and the fees are due in the first week of classes.","I plan to finish the degree in the library.","Funding is hard to find in the arts.","I'm hoping to land a teaching assistantship. It covers tuition and pays a stipend."], a: 3, x: "« How » demande un moyen. Les pièges parlent de calendrier, de lieu ou de généralités." },
    { id: "lza031", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "I'm leaning toward the thesis option, but I'd like to hear what you think.", o: ["I lean on the thesis when I walk.","Honestly, I'd go with it if you already have an idea you care about.","The option I like best is the cheapest one, since I'm trying to save for next term.","Honestly, I think you've heard enough from me."], a: 1, x: "On demande un avis : on le donne avec une condition. Pièges : lecture littérale, avis sur autre chose, refus incohérent." },
    { id: "lza032", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Would you mind if I sat in on your study group tonight?", o: ["Yes, we studied until about midnight.","I sat next to the window last time.","Not at all. The more, the merrier.","No, I don't think that statistic is right."], a: 2, x: "Après « Would you mind », « Not at all » = pas de problème. Les autres réponses n'ont aucun rapport avec la demande." },
    { id: "lza033", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "What's the deal with the new grading rubric? It makes no sense.", o: ["The deal was closed on Monday.","I know, right? Apparently clarity counts for more than content now.","It's a fair system, and the instructor explained it clearly.","The deal is that you need a B average to keep the scholarship this year."], a: 1, x: "« What's the deal with… » = qu'est-ce qui se passe avec. On acquiesce et on détaille. Pièges : sens littéral." },
    { id: "lza034", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Do you know if the chemistry lab is open to undergraduates after six?", o: ["Yes, I've taken chemistry for two terms.","The lab report is due by six on Friday.","Six students signed up for the lab session, and the instructor wanted more.","I think so, but you'll need your swipe card to get in."], a: 3, x: "Question indirecte sur l'accès : « I think so » + précision utile. Les pièges réutilisent « chemistry », « lab » ou « six » sans répondre." },
    { id: "lza035", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Have you picked a topic for your term paper yet?", o: ["Not quite. I'm torn between two, so I'm seeing my advisor tomorrow.","Yes, the paper is due on the twelfth.","I picked up the syllabus at the front desk, and the topics are listed on page two.","The term ended last week, so it's too late."], a: 0, x: "Question sur l'avancement : « Not quite » + justification. Les autres réponses répondent à « quand » ou répètent « picked » et « term »." },
    { id: "lza036", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "Between the lab and the part-time job, I barely have time to breathe.", o: ["The lab has excellent ventilation.","I breathe a lot better since I quit the job, but I miss the extra money.","You should talk to your advisor before you burn out.","Yes, the job is part of the lab."], a: 2, x: "Expression figurée de surcharge : on conseille d'agir. Piège : lecture littérale de « breathe »." },
    { id: "lza037", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "Our group presentation is on Friday, and half of us haven't even started.", o: ["We started the presentation on time yesterday.","Half of the slides are in the library folder, and the other half are still on my laptop.","Friday is when the presentations ended last term.","Then we'd better divide up the slides tonight and set a rehearsal for Thursday."], a: 3, x: "Constat d'un retard : on propose un plan. Pièges : mauvais temps, répétition de « half », « Friday »." },
    { id: "lza038", diff: 4, g: "M", p: "The professor's lecture was a masterclass in saying very little at great length.", o: ["I learned so much from it that I filled two notebooks.","Wasn't it? I filled two pages and couldn't tell you what the argument was.","Yes, she's well known for giving short, to-the-point lectures.","It was a masterclass, so the room was packed, and hardly anyone left before it ended."], a: 1, x: "Sarcasme : la conférence était longue et vide. On confirme. Le premier piège prend l'éloge au premier degré." },
    { id: "lza039", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "Do you know whether the writing center takes walk-ins, or do I have to book ahead?", o: ["They do on weekdays before noon. Otherwise you need an appointment.","I wrote in the center of the page.","The writing center is behind the main library.","Yes, I booked it ahead of time for you."], a: 0, x: "Question « ou » : réponse conditionnelle. « Walk-in » = sans rendez-vous." },
    { id: "lza040", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "My scholarship renewal depends on keeping a 3.5, and I'm barely above it.", o: ["I renewed my membership at the gym last week.","It's a generous scholarship, and it covers tuition, books, and even a monthly stipend.","That's a lot of pressure. Have you thought about getting a tutor?","Yes, I'm barely sure what a 3.5 means."], a: 2, x: "Inquiétude : on répond par de l'empathie et une suggestion. Les pièges répètent « renewal » ou « scholarship » sans réagir au souci." },
    { id: "lza041", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Is it better to email the professor or just show up at office hours?", o: ["Emails are sent to all the students.","Office hours are on the third floor, in the room next to the department secretary.","The professor showed up late yesterday.","I'd go in person. It's easier to explain things, and she seems to like it."], a: 3, x: "Demande de conseil avec choix : on choisit une option et on justifie. Les pièges répètent « email » ou « show up »." },
    { id: "lza042", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "I wouldn't be so quick to dismiss his results. The sample is small, but the trend is clear.", o: ["Good, then we can dismiss them right away.","He presented the results in a very small font.","Fair enough. I suppose I was mostly bothered by how he presented them.","The sample is in the freezer, as far as I know."], a: 2, x: "Nuance et concession : « Fair enough ». Les pièges contredisent l'avis ou jouent sur « small » et « sample »." },
    { id: "lza043", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "I couldn't make sense of the professor's feedback on my draft.", o: ["Why not ask her to go over it during office hours?","She makes a lot of sense in class.","The draft is due on the fifteenth.","I feel the same way about the weather."], a: 0, x: "Difficulté exprimée : on suggère une solution concrète. « Make sense » est répété dans un piège hors sujet." },
    { id: "lza044", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "Do you reckon the library will let us keep the study room past ten?", o: ["I reckon you'd keep better notes in that room.","It's worth asking at the desk. They've bent the rules during finals before.","Ten people are in the study room already, so I doubt there's space past ten.","The room is past the main stairs."], a: 1, x: "Question d'incertitude : on conseille de demander. Pièges : écho de « keep », « ten », « past »." },
    { id: "lza045", diff: 4, g: "W", p: "I'm not saying the data was fudged, but the error bars are suspiciously tidy.", o: ["That's a serious insinuation. Shouldn't we talk to the professor first?","I'm not saying that either, but the error bars look fine to me.","Right, tidy error bars are a sign of careful work, and a good reason to trust him.","The error bars are on the third figure, if you want to look."], a: 0, x: "« I'm not saying… but » insinue sans accuser. La bonne réponse relève la gravité. Pièges : on rejette l'insinuation, on prend « tidy » comme un compliment." },
    { id: "lza046", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "I'm thinking of joining the debate club. Have you ever been to a meeting?", o: ["I'm thinking of joining, too, but I'm not sure I have the time on Wednesday evenings.","The club fair takes place in the gym on Tuesday.","Once. Everyone was friendly, and they meet on Wednesday evenings.","I'm afraid the debate was cancelled last year."], a: 2, x: "« Have you ever » porte sur l'expérience : « Once » répond directement. Les autres réponses restent autour du club sans dire si la personne y est allée." },
    { id: "lza047", diff: 4, g: "W", p: "To say the grading was harsh would be putting it mildly.", o: ["Mild, yes. I got a B, which I was happy with.","It wasn't harsh at all, as far as I could tell.","I'd put it mildly, too, if I were talking to the dean, but I'm talking to you.","Tell me about it. Half the class got marked down for formatting alone."], a: 3, x: "« Putting it mildly » = c'était pire encore. On confirme avec un exemple. Pièges : contradiction (note correcte, pas dur)." },
    { id: "lza048", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "Would it be a problem if I turned in the lab write-up a day late?", o: ["I write everything up the day before.","It depends on the instructor, but you'd better ask before the deadline, not after.","I'd have written it up a day earlier.","A day late is the same as a day early."], a: 1, x: "Demande de permission : réponse nuancée (« It depends »). Pièges : temps verbal faux, raisonnement absurde, hors sujet." },
    { id: "lza049", diff: 4, g: "W", p: "I don't want to sound ungrateful, but is that really the best the department could offer?", o: ["I wondered the same. The stipend barely covers rent.","You don't sound ungrateful. It's an extremely generous package.","Yes, I'm grateful too. They offered me a lot.","The department could offer more if it had a bigger budget."], a: 0, x: "« I don't want to sound ungrateful, but… » précède une critique. On la partage avec un détail. Pièges : on nie le problème, on change de sujet." },
    { id: "lza050", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "I can't seem to get the regression to converge.", o: ["Regression analysis is covered in week eleven of the course, after the unit on sampling.","Have you tried standardizing the variables? That fixes it more often than not.","I can't seem to find a seat either.","I'm afraid the stats lab is closed until Monday."], a: 1, x: "Problème technique : conseil précis. Pièges : jeu de mots sans rapport." },
    { id: "lza051", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "I'm going to the career center to get my résumé reviewed.", o: ["I reviewed the movie last week.","My résumé is on the second page.","The career center is next to the gym, on the other side of the parking lot.","Good idea. Ask them about the alumni network, too."], a: 3, x: "Annonce d'une intention : approbation et conseil complémentaire. « Reviewed » est un piège de répétition." },
    { id: "lza052", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Excuse me, which office handles housing applications for next year?", o: ["I applied for a single room last month.","Next year's tuition has gone up by four percent, according to the notice on the board.","That would be Residential Life, on the ground floor of Hale Hall.","The housing market downtown is very competitive."], a: 2, x: "« Which office » appelle le nom d'un service (et un lieu). Les autres réponses restent dans le thème du logement sans répondre." },
    { id: "lza053", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "The department is cutting back on funding for travel to conferences.", o: ["Yes, the conference was cut short last year.","That's a blow. I'd been counting on presenting my poster in Chicago.","The back of the poster is made of cardboard.","Traveling is exciting when funding is available."], a: 1, x: "Mauvaise nouvelle : on réagit avec une conséquence personnelle. Les pièges répètent « cut » et « funding » sans réaction pertinente." },
    { id: "lza054", diff: 4, g: "W", p: "Not that I'm keeping score, but that's the third time this week the lab's been left in a mess.", o: ["I know, I've been keeping score of who uses the equipment most, I think.","It's not a competition, so I wouldn't worry about the numbers.","Third time? I'd say the cleaning crew is supposed to handle that.","Point taken. I'll make sure we clean up before we leave tonight."], a: 3, x: "« Not that I'm keeping score, but… » est un reproche déguisé ; on l'accepte et on s'engage. Les pièges prennent « score » au pied de la lettre ou renvoient la faute à d'autres." },
    { id: "lza055", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "I'm torn between writing a thesis and taking extra seminars instead.", o: ["I tore up my notes from the seminars.","The thesis seminar is on Wednesday afternoon, and it's open to all master's students.","It depends on what comes next. Are you aiming at a PhD or at a job in industry?","Instead of what? I didn't catch the question."], a: 2, x: "« Torn between » = hésiter. La bonne réponse aide à décider en posant la question pertinente. Piège : « tore »." },
    { id: "lza056", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Do you think I should take the morning section or the afternoon one?", o: ["If you're not a morning person, I'd go for the afternoon.","The section on tax law is at ten on Mondays, and the other one is at noon.","Both sections were full when I registered.","Morning sections are usually smaller than the afternoon ones."], a: 0, x: "Demande de conseil : recommandation conditionnelle. Les autres réponses donnent un fait voisin sans conseiller." },
    { id: "lza057", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "Do you mind if I ask what you got on the midterm? I'm trying to gauge where I stand.", o: ["Not at all. I got a ninety-one, but the class average was lower than I expected.","Honestly, I'd rather not stand in line again.","The midterm was held in the main hall, I think.","Yes, I got up early to study for it."], a: 0, x: "Après « Do you mind if », « Not at all » donne la permission, puis on répond. Les pièges jouent sur « stand » et « got »." },
    { id: "lza058", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "I got through the whole reading, but I can't say I retained much.", o: ["I always remember more when I read aloud, so I do that in the library at night.","Same here. Maybe we should compare notes and fill in the gaps together.","The whole class did the reading yesterday.","You should take your notes more slowly."], a: 1, x: "Aveu d'efficacité limitée : on s'identifie et on propose. Pièges : répétition." },
    { id: "lza059", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "Could you walk me through the process for appealing a grade?", o: ["I walked through the enrollment process last year.","The grade is posted on the board outside.","I'd appeal to the dean if I were walking by.","Sure. You start with the instructor, then file a form with the dean's office."], a: 3, x: "« Walk someone through » = expliquer pas à pas. Pièges : mauvais temps, sujet voisin sans explication." },
    { id: "lza060", diff: 4, g: "W", p: "I'd be the first to admit my model has its limits, but it's hardly useless.", o: ["I agree, it's useless at the moment, but we can fix it.","Then you should be the first to present it at the department seminar next week.","Nobody's saying it's useless. We just need to know where it breaks down.","Its limits are well documented in most textbooks, aren't they?"], a: 2, x: "« Hardly useless » = loin d'être inutile. La bonne réponse concède et déplace le débat vers les limites. Piège : contresens." },
    { id: "lza061", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Can I renew a library book online, or do I have to come in?", o: ["The library is on the second floor of the annex.","I renewed my passport online last month.","Yes, it's an interesting book, but quite long.","You can do it through your account, unless someone else has requested it."], a: 3, x: "Question à choix (« online, or come in ») : on retient la première option, avec une condition. « Renew » est répété dans une réponse hors sujet." },
    { id: "lza062", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Do you want to grab a table in the library before it fills up?", o: ["The table is made of oak, I believe.","Good thinking. Let's drop our bags and then get coffee.","It filled up quickly yesterday, so we missed the chance.","Yes, the library is full of tables."], a: 1, x: "Proposition : on l'accepte. Pièges : lecture littérale de « fills up » et mauvais temps verbal." },
    { id: "lza063", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "I'm not cut out for lab work, if I'm being honest.", o: ["You'd be perfect for it. You're so careful, and you always keep your bench so tidy.","Lab work was cut from the program.","Come on, you've only had a few sessions. Give it some time.","The lab is out of paper."], a: 2, x: "« Be cut out for » = avoir les qualités pour. On encourage. Pièges : sens littéral de « cut out »." },
    { id: "lza064", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Did the committee say when they'd announce the scholarship winners?", o: ["By the end of the month, I think, but they'll email everyone either way.","The scholarship is worth five thousand dollars.","I won a prize at a science fair once.","The announcement was made at the dean's office, in front of everyone who applied."], a: 0, x: "« When » demande une date : « By the end of the month ». Les autres sont sur le thème mais ne donnent pas de date." },
    { id: "lza065", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "Sorry to spring this on you, but could you cover my office hours on Thursday?", o: ["I'd love to, but I already covered that material in the last lecture.","No, I didn't spring any surprises on Thursday.","Sure, no problem. Just send me the sign-up sheet and anything I should know.","Of course. I'll cover the cost of the tickets."], a: 2, x: "« Spring this on you » = vous prévenir au dernier moment ; « cover » = remplacer. Les pièges prennent « cover » dans un autre sens (traiter un sujet, payer)." },
    { id: "lza066", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "Honestly, I could use a second pair of eyes on this abstract.", o: ["I've got a spare pair of glasses you can borrow.","Send it over. I'll read it tonight and mark anything that sounds unclear.","The abstract painting in the hall is lovely.","I'd rather see it in person at the exhibition."], a: 1, x: "« A second pair of eyes » = une relecture. Pièges : lecture littérale, double sens de « abstract »." },
    { id: "lza067", diff: 4, g: "M", p: "If the committee goes with the second proposal, we'll be back to square one.", o: ["Which is exactly why we should lobby for the first one this week.","Right, so the second proposal is the one we'd better support.","Then we'd better put a square in the first section.","We could go back to the committee once the second one passes and ask for changes."], a: 0, x: "« Back to square one » = repartir de zéro. La bonne réponse déduit qu'il faut défendre la première proposition. Pièges : inversion de logique." },
    { id: "lza068", diff: 4, g: "M", p: "At this rate, we'll be lucky to finish the first draft by the holidays.", o: ["We'll finish sooner than planned, then. That's lucky.","Yes, the holidays are a lucky time to finish something.","We were lucky to finish the first draft before the holidays last year, if I remember right.","I know. Maybe we should cut the third section and aim for something realistic."], a: 3, x: "« At this rate… lucky to » = pessimiste : on n'y arrivera sans doute pas. On propose de réduire. Pièges : contresens, mauvais temps." },
    { id: "lza069", diff: 4, g: "M", p: "We might as well not have bothered applying, given the odds.", o: ["Don't be so negative. Somebody has to win, and it might as well be us.","Those odds sound good. When do we hear back?","I applied twice, and the odds were noticeably better the second time around, I think.","The odds were stated clearly on the application form, I think."], a: 0, x: "« Might as well not have bothered » = inutile de s'être donné la peine. La bonne réponse relativise. Pièges : accord pessimiste, mauvais sujet, conseil incohérent." },
    { id: "lza070", diff: 4, g: "W", p: "I could do without the group work, to be perfectly honest.", o: ["I couldn't do it without you. You're so organized.","The group work is the best part of the course, I think.","Same here. Somebody always ends up carrying the rest.","Perfectly honest, yes. Your work is perfectly fine, I suppose."], a: 2, x: "« Could do without » = préférer s'en passer. On partage l'avis. Pièges : sens inversé (« couldn't do without »)." },
    { id: "lza071", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "Remind me why we signed up for an eight a.m. class?", o: ["I remind you every morning at eight.","Signing up was a mistake in the first place.","Eight students are enrolled in that section.","Because it was the only section that didn't clash with our other classes."], a: 3, x: "Question rhétorique d'agacement : on donne la raison. Les autres répètent « remind », « eight »." },
    { id: "lza072", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Would you be so kind as to point me toward the thesis office?", o: ["I'm very kind to the thesis students.","Of course. Go past the cafeteria, and it's the second door on your left.","Yes, I'd be glad to point out the main details in your thesis, if you'd like me to.","The office hours start at ten."], a: 1, x: "Demande de direction polie : on donne le chemin. Les pièges jouent sur « kind », « point » et « office »." },
    { id: "lza073", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "Look, I hate to be the bearer of bad news, but your sample was contaminated.", o: ["Seriously? That means I'll have to rerun the whole experiment.","Thanks for bearing the news to the team.","Yes, the sample is a very good one.","I'm glad to hear the news is good."], a: 0, x: "Annonce de mauvaise nouvelle : réaction et conséquence. Pièges : contresens de la nouvelle." },
    { id: "lza074", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "Do you think Professor Klein would be open to supervising a thesis on behavioral finance?", o: ["She's open from nine to five on weekdays, except during the faculty meeting on Thursdays.","It's worth a shot. She's just published a paper on loss aversion.","I think behavior is shaped by finance.","That thesis was supervised by someone else last year."], a: 1, x: "« Be open to » = être ouvert à (une idée), pas « ouvert » (horaires). Le premier piège joue sur le sens littéral." },
    { id: "lza075", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Is the study room on the third floor free, or has it been booked?", o: ["The third floor was renovated recently.","I booked a flight for the third of May.","It's free until two, and then a group has it reserved.","It filled up quickly yesterday, so we missed our chance."], a: 2, x: "Question « ou » : la réponse donne la disponibilité exacte. Piège : « booked » détourné, temps du passé hors sujet." },
    { id: "lza076", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "I was hoping you'd have had a chance to look over my proposal by now.", o: ["You'll have plenty of chances before the deadline.","I hope you'll get a chance to look over mine, too.","Yes, the proposal looked very promising to everyone.","I'm so sorry. It slipped through the cracks. I'll get to it tonight."], a: 3, x: "« I was hoping you'd have… by now » est un reproche indirect : on s'excuse et on s'engage. Les pièges inversent les rôles ou répondent comme à un compliment." },
    { id: "lza077", diff: 4, g: "W", p: "Were it not for the extension, I'd have missed the submission window altogether.", o: ["Lucky you. Mine got denied, so I was up all night.","So you did miss it, then? What happened?","That's the problem with windows. They always close.","Yes, without the extension I would not have missed it."], a: 0, x: "« Were it not for… » : sans la prolongation elle aurait raté la date. La bonne réponse réagit à la chance. Pièges : contresens de la condition." },
    { id: "lza078", diff: 4, g: "W", p: "I fail to see why we should have to defend the methodology twice.", o: ["You failed to defend it the first time, that's why.","It does seem excessive. Maybe the second reviewer didn't read the first report.","We defended it twice and passed both times.","It's the methodology section that I find hardest to defend."], a: 1, x: "« I fail to see why » = je ne comprends pas pourquoi. La bonne réponse propose une explication plausible. Pièges : prise littérale de « fail »." },
    { id: "lza079", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "You haven't happened to see a flash drive around here, have you? It's got my whole thesis on it.", o: ["No, I don't have any hard drives at home.","The thesis is due on the first of May.","Yes, the flash flood damaged the library.","Oh no. What color is it? I'll check the printer room and ask at the front desk."], a: 3, x: "Demande d'aide urgente : on propose de chercher. Pièges : écho « drive », échéance sans rapport, mot « flash » détourné." },
    { id: "lza080", diff: 4, g: "W", p: "I'd say the defense could have gone worse, but I'd have to think hard about how.", o: ["That's a relief. Did the committee single out anything for praise?","I'm surprised they let you off so easily, then.","That bad? Well, at least it's behind you now.","I suppose I'd have to think hard about how, too."], a: 2, x: "Ironie : « could have gone worse, but I'd have to think hard » = la soutenance s'est très mal passée. Les pièges la lisent au premier degré (succès) ou répètent la phrase." },
    { id: "lza081", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "She aced the oral exam, and she hardly prepared for it.", o: ["I'm glad she prepared so thoroughly.","I'd hardly call it luck. She studied for two weeks.","Some people have all the luck. I spent two weeks on mine and just scraped by.","It was an oral exam, so no writing was needed, and she had a very friendly examiner."], a: 2, x: "« Hardly » = presque pas. Deux pièges contredisent l'énoncé (elle avait peu préparé)." },
    { id: "lza082", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "The seminar room is locked, and nobody seems to have the key.", o: ["The seminar was held in a closed session, which is why the doors are locked on Fridays.","Let's ask the department secretary. She usually keeps a spare.","I usually leave my keys in the dorm room.","Yes, the secretary seems quite friendly."], a: 1, x: "Constat d'un problème : on propose une solution. Les pièges reprennent « locked », « key » ou « secretary » sans proposer d'issue." },
    { id: "lza083", diff: 4, g: "M", p: "I'll believe the refurbished lab is ready by September when I see it.", o: ["I know what you mean. They promised the same thing two years ago and missed the date by months.","Good, then you'll see it in September, as they said.","Believe me, it'll be ready by September. I saw the contractors working on it yesterday afternoon.","I'll believe it when I see it, too, but I don't need the lab."], a: 0, x: "« I'll believe it when I see it » = scepticisme. La bonne réponse le partage avec un précédent. Pièges : confiance contraire, répétition sans apport." },
    { id: "lza084", diff: 4, g: "W", p: "Frankly, I'd be amazed if anyone passed that exam without cramming.", o: ["Most people pass it easily, which honestly amazes me, given how hard the questions look.","I'm amazed at how many people stay up cramming.","It's an amazing exam, I must say, and a fair one.","Tell me about it. I've been up since five, and I'm still not through chapter six."], a: 3, x: "« I'd be amazed if anyone… » = personne n'y arrive sans bachoter. On confirme avec une anecdote. Pièges : contradiction (« pass it easily ») ou écho d'« amazed »." },
    { id: "lza085", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "I wish I'd taken the course with Professor Hale when I had the chance.", o: ["I wish I had the chance to take the course, but I've got too many credits already.","I chanced upon Hale on the street yesterday.","She has wished to teach the course for years.","It's not too late, is it? She's teaching it again in the spring."], a: 3, x: "« I wish I'd… » exprime un regret. On répond avec une solution. Les pièges répètent « wish », « chance »." },
    { id: "lza086", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Excuse me, are you the teaching assistant for the economics course?", o: ["No, that's Daniel. He's usually in room 214 on Tuesdays.","Yes, the economics course is full this term.","I assist the librarian in the evenings.","The course is taught on Tuesdays and Thursdays, in the large hall on the main floor."], a: 0, x: "Question oui/non sur une identité : « No » + renseignement utile. Les pièges répètent « course » ou « Tuesdays »." },
    { id: "lza087", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "I don't suppose you'd be able to lend me your notes from last Tuesday?", o: ["I suppose Tuesday was last week.","Of course. I'll scan them and send them over this evening.","I'd be able to supply you with a pen.","I suppose you're right about the lecture."], a: 1, x: "« I don't suppose… » = demande très polie. Pièges : écho de « suppose » et « able »." },
    { id: "lza088", diff: 4, g: "W", p: "I'm in two minds about whether to report him for plagiarism.", o: ["Yes, he's been reported to the integrity office twice already.","Two minds are better than one, so ask a friend.","It's a hard call. It might be worth talking to the integrity office first, informally.","He plagiarized my paper two minutes ago."], a: 2, x: "« In two minds » = hésiter. La bonne réponse conseille une démarche prudente. Pièges : conseils tranchés qui ignorent l'hésitation." },
    { id: "lza089", diff: 4, g: "M", p: "Not to belabor the point, but we do have to finalize the budget today.", o: ["Yes, the budget was finalized yesterday afternoon, I believe, at the finance meeting.","It's a fine point, but I wouldn't belabor it.","I know. Let's go through the remaining items and be done with it by five.","I'd finalize it, but I don't know the figures."], a: 2, x: "« Not to belabor the point » = sans vouloir insister. On accepte la pression et on propose un plan. Pièges : mauvais temps, refus déguisé." },
    { id: "lza090", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "I only just found out the grant application needs a letter from the dean.", o: ["The grant was supported by a private donor.","I support the dean's decision on that matter, since the process has always been fair.","The letter arrived in the mail on Tuesday.","That could be tricky. Her calendar fills up weeks in advance."], a: 3, x: "Constat d'une difficulté : on commente la complication. Les pièges répètent « letter », « grant » ou « dean »." },
    { id: "lza091", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "Should we print the poster on campus, or is it cheaper at a copy shop?", o: ["The copy shop downtown is cheaper, but the campus print center is faster.","Yes, we should print it on campus.","The poster has a lot of color, so the print center might charge extra for it.","I campus-printed it for you yesterday."], a: 0, x: "Question à choix : on compare les deux options. « Yes » à une question « or » est une erreur classique." },
    { id: "lza092", diff: 4, g: "W", p: "He talks a good game, but I've yet to see him deliver anything.", o: ["He's delivered quite a lot, as far as I can tell.","That's been my impression, too. Lots of promises, very little follow-through.","I've never heard him make a single promise, to be honest, so I can't say he's failed.","Actually, he doesn't talk much at all in meetings."], a: 1, x: "« Talk a good game » = être fort en paroles seulement. On abonde. Pièges : contradiction, jeu sur « game », fait faux." },
    { id: "lza093", diff: 4, g: "M", p: "For better or worse, the thesis is finished.", o: ["It's definitely for the better. Your supervisor must be thrilled.","Worse, I'd say. It needs another round of revisions.","Better or worse than what? I didn't catch the comparison.","Congratulations, anyway. Now you can finally sleep."], a: 3, x: "« For better or worse » = quoi qu'on en pense : sentiment mitigé. « Anyway » reconnaît la réserve. Pièges : choix tranché ou incompréhension de l'idiome." },
    { id: "lza094", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "I'd like to know what the late-submission policy is for the final project.", o: ["The final project is worth forty percent of the grade.","Papers handed in within a day lose ten percent; after that, they're not accepted.","Submissions are accepted in the main hall.","I handed mine in ahead of time."], a: 1, x: "Demande d'information sur un règlement : la bonne réponse l'explique. Les autres donnent un détail voisin (note, lieu, expérience personnelle)." },
    { id: "lza095", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "Would you say it's worth buying a used textbook, or are the editions too different?", o: ["Last year's edition is fine. The pages differ, but the content's basically the same.","Used books are sold at the corner store near the gate, usually at half the price of new ones.","The editions are published by the university press.","Yes, I'd say the textbooks were worth it."], a: 0, x: "Question à choix : on tranche et on justifie. Les autres restent autour des manuels." },
    { id: "lza096", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "Do you have a sec? I'm stuck on question four of the problem set.", o: ["I stuck my answer to question four on the board.","Four of us finished the set early.","Sure. Let me see what you've got so far.","Problem sets are usually due on Fridays."], a: 2, x: "« A sec » = un instant ; « stuck » = bloqué. Pièges : jeu sur « stuck » et « four »." },
    { id: "lza097", diff: 4, g: "W", p: "It's one thing to propose a policy and quite another to see it through.", o: ["Yes, it's a proposal I'm quite happy to see through.","I agree, which is why I proposed a quite different policy.","Proposing policies is the committee's job, though.","Right, and in this department, good ideas tend to die in committee."], a: 3, x: "« One thing… quite another » : proposer ≠ mener à bien. On abonde avec un exemple concret. Pièges : écho de « propose » et « quite »." },
    { id: "lza098", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "If I were you, I'd get the outline to Dr. Ortiz before the break.", o: ["If you were me, you'd understand how little time I have.","Dr. Ortiz broke her leg last winter, so she was away from campus for months.","You're right. Once the semester ends, she's impossible to pin down.","The outline is stuck in the printer."], a: 2, x: "« If I were you » introduit un conseil. On l'accepte en ajoutant une raison. Pièges : contresens sur l'hypothèse, écho « break » / « broke »." },
    { id: "lza099", diff: 4, g: "M", p: "You'd think they'd have the decency to post the schedule before registration opens.", o: ["Tell me about it. I've been refreshing that page all morning.","Well, registration does open at eight, so it should appear soon.","They've been decent about it, honestly. The schedule was posted on time.","I'd post it myself if I had access to the site."], a: 0, x: "« You'd think… » exprime l'agacement face à une négligence ; « Tell me about it » = je suis d'accord. Pièges : prise au pied de la lettre, contradiction (« posted on time »), offre décalée." },
    { id: "lza100", diff: 4, g: "M", p: "With all due respect, I think the committee is missing the point.", o: ["With respect, the committee has made its point clearly enough.","That may be, but I'd choose my words carefully before saying so in the meeting.","Then you should apologize to them in public.","The point of the meeting is to hear everyone's opinion."], a: 1, x: "« With all due respect » introduit un désaccord poli. La bonne réponse l'admet et conseille la prudence. Pièges : écho de « respect » et « point », conseil déplacé." },
    { id: "lza101", diff: 4, g: "M", p: "He might have a point, but he certainly has a funny way of making it.", o: ["Exactly. If he were less abrasive, people might actually listen.","It was funny, wasn't it? Everyone laughed when he made that remark in the lecture.","He did make a good point, and I think it was well put.","His way of making it was original. I'd like to hear more, to be honest."], a: 0, x: "« A funny way of » = une façon déroutante (critique). La bonne réponse l'interprète comme un défaut de ton. Pièges : « funny » = drôle." },
    { id: "lza102", diff: 4, g: "M", p: "The best I can say for the lecture is that the coffee was decent.", o: ["I'm glad you enjoyed the lecture, though.","The best coffee is on the third floor, near the library.","Yes, the coffee helps when the lecture is long.","Ouch. Was it really that bad?"], a: 3, x: "Litote : la conférence était mauvaise. « Ouch » + relance. Pièges : lecture positive, détour sur le café." },
    { id: "lza103", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "Would it be out of line to ask Dr. Weiss for a recommendation after only one semester?", o: ["She was out of the line for the whole semester.","Yes, one semester is enough for Dr. Weiss.","Not at all, as long as you give her plenty of notice and a copy of your résumé.","A recommendation for a restaurant is easy to get, especially in a college town like this one."], a: 2, x: "« Out of line » = déplacé. « Not at all » = non, ce n'est pas déplacé. Le piège « Yes » dit l'inverse." },
    { id: "lza104", diff: 4, g: "W", p: "I wouldn't say the group project was a disaster, exactly.", o: ["That's great. So you're all happy with the final grade?","I'll take that as a polite way of saying it went badly.","Why exactly would anyone say it was a disaster?","Right, a project like that is hard to judge exactly."], a: 1, x: "« I wouldn't say… exactly » est un euphémisme : le projet a mal tourné. Les pièges lisent la phrase comme un succès ou la prennent comme une vraie question." },
    { id: "lza105", diff: 4, g: "M", p: "It's not so much that the thesis is weak as that it never quite commits to a claim.", o: ["So you'd like me to sharpen the argument rather than gather more evidence?","I'm glad you think the argument is strong. I'll gather a bit more evidence anyway.","Then I should probably add a few more citations to the weakest chapters, I suppose.","Right, so the committee will want a fuller literature review."], a: 0, x: "« Not so much A as B » : le défaut est B (absence de thèse nette), pas la faiblesse des preuves. La bonne réponse reformule exactement cela ; les pièges corrigent A (preuves, citations, bibliographie)." },
    { id: "lza106", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "He's been dodging my emails for a week.", o: ["He dodged the ball very well when we played volleyball at orientation last week.","That's frustrating. Maybe try catching him right after class?","I've been sending emails for a week as well.","The week's emails are on the board."], a: 1, x: "« Dodge » = esquiver. On compatit et on suggère. Pièges : sens sportif, répétition." },
    { id: "lza107", diff: 4, g: "W", p: "She's the sort of advisor who'll tell you your idea is brilliant and then quietly bury it.", o: ["Well, if she says it's brilliant, you should keep working on it.","I'd rather have an advisor who buries ideas than one who copies them.","That's the worst kind. At least a flat no lets you move on.","She sounds supportive. I wish mine praised my ideas, too."], a: 2, x: "Critique implicite d'une approbation de façade. On convient qu'un non franc est préférable. Pièges : lecture naïve de « brilliant », hors sujet." },
    { id: "lza108", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "Is there any chance I could swap into your discussion section? Mine clashes with my job.", o: ["I swapped the sections of the book on my desk.","My job is fine. It pays well enough, and the manager is flexible with my hours around exams.","Discussions are always better in small sections.","I think so, but you'd have to check with the TA, since there's a cap on enrollment."], a: 3, x: "Demande de changement : « I think so » + condition. « Clash » = conflit d'horaires. Les pièges ignorent la demande." },
    { id: "lza109", diff: 4, g: "M", p: "The funding committee keeps asking for impact, whatever that means.", o: ["Right? Last year I just wrote a vague paragraph about policy relevance, and it worked.","It means the measurable effect of your research, so you should include figures, to be honest.","They're giving funding to projects with the biggest impact, I think, so aim for the largest effect.","Impact is important, which is why the committee asks about it."], a: 0, x: "« Whatever that means » : scepticisme face à un mot à la mode. La bonne réponse le partage avec une anecdote. Les pièges prennent le mot au sérieux et l'expliquent." },
    { id: "lza110", diff: 4, g: "M", p: "Do you think anyone would notice if I slipped out before the end of the talk?", o: ["Yes, I noticed it when the talk slipped past five.","Probably not, but the speaker is your advisor's friend, so I wouldn't risk it.","The end of the talk is at five, so you'd still have plenty of time for coffee afterward.","No one noticed me slipping in, either."], a: 1, x: "Question hypothétique : « Probably not, but… » + prudence. Pièges : jeu sur « notice » et « slip »." },
    { id: "lza111", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "How did you do on the statistics quiz?", o: ["It was a short quiz, only about twenty minutes, and most people finished early.","I took the quiz at the library yesterday.","Better than I'd feared, though I made a couple of silly mistakes.","The statistics come from last year's survey."], a: 2, x: "« How did you do » demande le résultat, pas la durée ni le lieu." },
    { id: "lza112", diff: 4, g: "W", p: "He's hardly the first student to plead ignorance of the citation rules.", o: ["Right, so he's likely to be the first one the committee treats leniently.","Yes, he should plead the rules to the committee himself.","I'm not sure he's ignorant of the rules, but he knows the committee well.","True, but I doubt the committee will accept that as an excuse."], a: 3, x: "« Hardly the first » = loin d'être le premier : l'excuse est banale. La bonne réponse en tire la conséquence. Les pièges contredisent ou déforment le sens." },
    { id: "lza113", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "I heard the department is considering making the statistics prerequisite stricter.", o: ["The statistics department is on the fourth floor.","They considered it before and decided against it.","I heard that on the radio during the strike last spring, but nobody confirmed it.","That'd be a headache for anyone who hasn't taken it yet. Does it start next fall?"], a: 3, x: "Rumeur : réaction sur les conséquences. Pièges : écho." },
    { id: "lza114", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "That's the second time this month the Wi-Fi's gone down in the middle of an online exam.", o: ["It's unacceptable. We should file a complaint with IT together.","I'd go down to the exam room with you, if you like, and wait in the hallway.","The second exam is next month.","I took the exam in the middle of the room."], a: 0, x: "Plainte : on la partage et on propose une action. Pièges : mots répétés (« down », « second », « middle »)." },
    { id: "lza115", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Would you rather do your internship in finance or in consulting?", o: ["Yes, I'd rather study in the library.","Finance, probably. It's closer to what I'm studying.","The internship starts in June.","I interned at a bank last summer, and the pay was good."], a: 1, x: "« Would you rather… or… » demande un choix : on nomme une option. Les pièges répondent par oui ou changent de sujet." },
    { id: "lza116", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "I'm having trouble finding enough sources for my literature review.", o: ["I read three reviews of that novel last week.","The library closes at ten tonight.","Have you tried interlibrary loan? They can get almost anything.","The review I read was published in a literary journal back in the spring."], a: 2, x: "Problème : on propose une aide concrète. « Review » et « library » sont des pièges de répétition." },
    { id: "lza117", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "I've half a mind to switch labs.", o: ["Half of the lab is switched off right now.","I've a mind to join you, then.","What's holding you back? Is it the new supervisor?","The lab is half empty today."], a: 2, x: "« Have half a mind to » = avoir bien envie de. Pièges : lecture littérale de « half » et « switch »." },
    { id: "lza118", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "I've been bouncing between the library and the lab all day, and I haven't eaten.", o: ["No wonder you look drained. Let me buy you a sandwich.","I eat lunch in the lab all the time, so I'm used to skipping the cafeteria.","The library had a basketball court once.","Don't bounce around. Just pick one place to study, to be honest."], a: 0, x: "« No wonder » = pas étonnant. Réponse empathique et utile. Pièges : lecture littérale de « bouncing »." },
    { id: "lza119", diff: 4, g: "W", p: "I take it you didn't get the fellowship, then.", o: ["Yes, I take it that the fellowship was very generous.","Not this time. They said the competition was fierce.","I got it, and I'm delighted, thanks.","Take it easy. The fellowship is for graduates only."], a: 1, x: "« I take it… » = je suppose que. La bonne réponse confirme. Pièges : confusion « Yes » / « I take it », contradiction." },
    { id: "lza120", diff: 4, g: "W", p: "Honestly, you can lead a student to the library, but you can't make them read.", o: ["The library has plenty of books to lead them on.","Actually, I make my study group read every week.","No, but you can make them quiet, which helps.","Ha, true. I've stopped nagging my study group about it."], a: 3, x: "Proverbe adapté : on ne peut pas forcer quelqu'un à apprendre. La bonne réponse adhère avec humour. Pièges : contradiction, détournement." },
    { id: "lza121", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "I'd have thought the registrar would've sorted out my transcript by now.", o: ["I thought the transcript was lost, too.","The registrar has sorted the files by name.","I'd have preferred a different transcript.","You'd think so. Have you tried calling them rather than emailing?"], a: 3, x: "« I'd have thought… » exprime l'agacement : on acquiesce (« You'd think so ») et on propose une piste. Les pièges répètent « thought » et « sorted »." },
    { id: "lza122", diff: 4, g: "M", p: "She's about as helpful as a chocolate teapot.", o: ["I'll ask her tomorrow, then. She's in the office at nine.","That's helpful to know. I'll buy a teapot, too.","That bad? I'd go to the TA instead, then.","Well, a chocolate teapot is quite sweet, actually."], a: 2, x: "Comparaison idiomatique : très peu utile. La bonne réponse décode et en tire une conclusion. Pièges : contresens, lecture littérale." },
    { id: "lza123", diff: 4, g: "W", p: "Say what you like about the library renovation, but they've finally fixed the heating.", o: ["You can say what you like, but I've already said everything I wanted to about it.","Fair point. I'll give them that. It's the first time I've been warm in there.","Say what you like. They never fixed anything.","The renovation was fixed last week, I believe."], a: 1, x: "« Say what you like, but… » = quoi qu'on pense du reste. On concède le point positif. Pièges : contradiction, mélange." }
  );
})();
